# r1113 Power Grid boot on jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar (sha1 cbc2ddee37ca, port
# phase 10: all content; copper plating, ceiling tiles and attachments, string light cord; fixes B30 to B34).
# Supersedes pwg16.qb (verdicts: perf/runs/r1113/verdicts/pwg16.md). One boot, one batch, this order:
#   1. SQ-PWG-90 boot row: version 19.2-17, phase 10, ns counts, 116 recipes, zpwg10 check (B33, B34), zpwg5 nbtall
#      (57 structures incl. ceiling_tile and wire/string_lights). The version / phase / count expects of the rerun rows
#      (SQ-PWG-84, -72, -76) are here, on the -17 numbers.
#   2. P10 rows in the queue's run order: SQ-PWG-91, -95, -92, -93, -94, -96 (CQ-PWG-28 / -29 are client rows), then
#      SQ-PWG-SHOW17 (not a row: lit string lights, a plating wall and a lit ceiling left for cq_pwg17.qb's tour)
#   3. reruns of the pwg16 BATCH-FAULT / INCONCLUSIVE rows, with the fixes:
#      SQ-PWG-84 (zpwg9b / 9c / 9d check: Forge tag lookups, recipe type from the recipe manager, Unbreaking by NBT)
#      SQ-PWG-72 (zpwg9b check), SQ-PWG-73 (cord with step lines, menus closed between packets), SQ-PWG-76 (zpwg9b / 9c
#      check, chain board), SQ-PWG-78 (again: it makes the schematic the chain needs), -79 to -83 (copper deployers
#      hold immersiveengineering:plate_copper, the pack's only #forge:plates/copper item; mixer and arm driven through
#      a gearbox; loop stops after 8 cycles), SQ-PWG-85 (Unbreaking), SQ-PWG-88 (pigs, not MCA villagers and a
#      peaceful-world witch), SQ-PWG-89 (twice, the byproduct chance is 20 %), SQ-PWG-63 (p8 calls the display's use
#      directly: Create's value box handler replays fake-player clicks at the block centre)
#   SQ-PWG-57, -74, -75, -77, -86, -87 passed in pwg16 and are not repeated.
# Group A superflat, level pwg17, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61 (grass), blocks at Y -60. Each area's SETUP row kills
# the animals generated in its chunks (box selector). The world is peaceful (no hostile mobs: no witch, see SQ-PWG-88).
# Areas (no block overlap):
#   P10    X 1095 to 1135, Z 1995 to 2085 (SQ-PWG-90 forceload; -91 Z 2010, -92 2020 to 2023, -93 2030 to 2043, -94 2050,
#          -95 2060, -96 2069 to 2070; SHOW17 (client tour) X 1100 to 1123, Z 2010 to 2017 and 2080 to 2084)
#   ponder X 1290 to 1990, Z 1290 to 1320 (SQ-PWG-90, zpwg5 nbtall at 1300 -60 1300, 57 structures 12 apart)
#   P9d    X 1095 to 1200, Z 1920 to 1990 (SQ-PWG-84 forceload; -85 Z 1929 to 1940, -88 Z 1963 to 1976, -89 Z 1984 to 1988)
#   P9b    X 1090 to 1130, Z 1805 to 1850 (SQ-PWG-72 forceload; -73 Z 1810 to 1825)
#   P9c    X 1135 to 1200, Z 1855 to 1915 (SQ-PWG-76 forceload; mixer gearboxes and motors at Y -57, Z 1889 to 1890;
#          arm gearboxes at Y -61 under the arms, motors one block north of them)
#   P8     X 1290 to 1320, Z 1590 to 1615 (SETUP63; SQ-PWG-63 Z 1598 to 1609)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwg17 A spawn-animals=true
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar: remove -16 and
#     older); sha1sum of the jar starts cbc2ddee37ca
#   for p in $INST/tools/scratch_query/pwg_*.js; do cp "$p" OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$(basename "$p"); done
#     (thirteen probes, the CURRENT copies: pwg_probe, pwg_grid_probe, pwg_p3 to p8, pwg_p9a to p9d, pwg_p10)
#   ls OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_*.js | wc -l      (13)
#   grep -c 'COPPER_PLATE\|vdrive' OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_pwg_p9c_probe.js   (non-zero: the pwg17 p9c)
#   ponder datapack from the -17 jar (79 structure files; SQ-PWG-90 places 57 of them through zpwg5):
#   rm -rf OUT/pwgp; mkdir -p OUT/pwgp OUT/srv/pwg17/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures \
#     && unzip -o -q OUT/srv/mods/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar 'assets/powergrid/ponder/*' -d OUT/pwgp \
#     && cp -r OUT/pwgp/assets/powergrid/ponder/. OUT/srv/pwg17/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures/ \
#     && printf '{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG ponder structures, scratch only"}}' > OUT/srv/pwg17/datapacks/pwgponder/pack.mcmeta
#   find OUT/srv/pwg17/datapacks/pwgponder -name '*.nbt' | wc -l      (79)
#   Loading Protection (shorter protection window, as pwg10 to pwg16):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Nothing else: no CC program, no other datapack, no config edit.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg17.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwg17
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
# Batch deviations from the row text: tick waits are sleeps; CONSUME accepted beside SUCCESS; SQ-PWG-90 checks 57
# structures (the p5 probe carries 57; the 79 files are all in the datapack, the P8 and P9a ones were placed by zpwg8 /
# zpwg9 in earlier boots); SQ-PWG-95's dye colours are a look (each channel may read one lower); SQ-PWG-88 on pigs (a pig
# with 26 max health stands in for the witch).
pace 1

